    "created_at": "2018-04-06T18:13:26Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-06T18:13:26Z",
    "body": "The suggested change to `<fieldset>` behaviour would make it impossible for a child `<input>` element of `<fieldset>` to be directly set to a different `<form>` using `form` attribute, where a `<fieldset>` `form` attribute is set to a specific `<form>` `id`, correct?\r\n\r\n```\r\n    <form id=\"formIncludingFieldset\" method=\"POST\" action=\"/echo/html/\">\r\n      <fieldset form=\"formIncludingFieldset\" name=\"fieldsetName0\">\r\n        <legend>fieldsetName</legend>\r\n        <input type=\"text\" name=\"input0\" value=\"123\" form=\"formIncludingInputWithFormAttrReferencingAnotherForm\">\r\n      </fieldset>\r\n      <input type=\"submit\">\r\n    </form>\r\n    \r\n        <form id=\"formIncludingInputWithFormAttrReferencingAnotherForm\" method=\"POST\" action=\"/echo/html/\">\r\n      <fieldset form=\"formIncludingInputWithFormAttrReferencingAnotherForm\" name=\"fieldsetName1\">\r\n        <legend>fieldsetName</legend>\r\n        <input type=\"text\" name=\"input1\" value=\"456\" form=\"formIncludingFieldset\">\r\n      </fieldset>\r\n      <input type=\"submit\">\r\n    </form>\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhat is the issue with iterating control elements and setting `form` element directly?\r\n\r\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
