    "created_at": "2018-04-06T19:45:29Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-04-06T19:45:38Z",
    "body": "Correct.\r\nThe main issue I see with iterating control elements is that you'd require a script for an HTML form which might otherwise not need a single bit of JS - Forms are often self-contained in the frontend via HTML/CSS.  \r\n\r\nI think what it comes down to, is that this is an _enhancement_ of the attribute - bringing it up to par with the power of a fieldset's `disabled`.  To me, the `form` attribute on a fieldset seems quite useless otherwise.",
